We can easily obtain the equilibrium concentrations of reactants and products once we have obtained the positive root of the equilibrium polynomial, the extent of the reaction. Let us analyze the reaction between water and carbon monoxide to produce carbon dioxide and hydrogen given that the initial concentration of water is 0.2M and the one for carbon monoxide is 0.1M
